# ===== The Veil: passive texts after the in-game test (2026-10-07) =====
# The Veil names every source of Doubt and Distortion's Double; Two Truths says the Mirror spells deal half (D17).
@loca h8cce4774gc43ag85c1gfbf4g7a2213dd6822 <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Target_Arcana_Card_Spell_MirrorImage">Mirror Image</LSTag> and <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Target_Arcana_Card_Spell_Distortion">Distortion</LSTag> summon Doubles: illusions of you with 1 <LSTag Tooltip="HitPoints">hit point</LSTag> that act on their own turn and can <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Shout_Deceiver_Double_Shatter">Shatter</LSTag>. You can keep 3 Doubles at once, 4 from level 7 and 5 from level 12, and you gain +1 <LSTag Tooltip="ArmourClass">Armour Class</LSTag> for each one.<br><br>Your illusions sow <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_1">Doubt</LSTag>. An enemy gains it when it destroys a Double, when a Shatter hits it, when your <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="SIGIL">Sigil</LSTag> detonates on it and when <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Target_Arcana_Card_Spell_MaliciousWhispers">Malicious Whispers</LSTag> hits it while marked. At 3 stacks it becomes <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DELUDED">Deluded</LSTag>.<br><br>Your Doubles vanish when combat ends, after a <LSTag Tooltip="LongRest">Long Rest</LSTag> or if you die.
@loca h044da674g7686g830dg2f87g5b39f2ff46e4 Your Doubles can also cast <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Projectile_Deceiver_Double_MirrorSigil">Mirror: Sigil of Malice</LSTag> and <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Target_Deceiver_Double_MirrorChains">Mirror: Ethereal Chains</LSTag>. Both deal half the damage of your <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Projectile_Arcana_Card_Spell_SigilofMalice">Sigil of Malice</LSTag> at your highest spell slot.
